WEBVTT
NOTE Cedwyn film, frame 003, en. Timings estimated from the script.

1
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:19.538
<v a Romano-British farmer>Good spelt this year. Dry enough to thresh before the rain comes up the valley. Look, smoke over the brow. They've the fires lit up at the stone house already.

2
00:00:19.888 --> 00:00:30.658
<v a Romano-British farm woman>Then thresh it quick. The quern's hungry, and so are the children. Fine red pots from far off, and we still eat the same porridge out of them.

3
00:00:31.008 --> 00:00:38.700
<v a Romano-British farmer>Gran used to tell us her people kept a round house right here. Now it's the barn and the oxen.

4
00:00:39.050 --> 00:00:53.665
<v a Romano-British farm woman>Call them in, then. There's cloud coming up off the marsh. And the geese are fat this year: one for the turn of the year, and one for your mother, or we'll never hear the end of it.

5
00:00:54.015 --> 00:00:58.246
<v a Romano-British farmer>Let them run. The hill's big enough for all of us.
